# www serves a complete duplicate of the site under HTTP 200. Every page's
# canonical tag points at the apex, so Google consolidates rather than indexing
# both, but it still spends crawl budget fetching the duplicate: the www copies
# are what most of the 64 "Alternative page with proper canonical tag" URLs are,
# on a site already sitting on 1,629 discovered-but-not-indexed URLs.
#
# A 301 settles it at the edge instead of asking the crawler to work it out.
# Cloudflare Pages matches on the full URL when the source includes a scheme
# and host; the 301! forces the redirect even where a static file exists.
https://www.ukelections.co.uk/* https://ukelections.co.uk/:splat 301!
